<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish unemployment falls to s/a 256,000 in April.</title>
<headline>Irish unemployment falls to s/a 256,000 in April.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of those claiming Irish unemployment benefit fell to a seasonally-adjusted 256,000 in April from 260,600 in March, Central Statistics Office (CSO) figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, the numbers claiming benefit fell to 255,463 from 262,414 in March.</p>
<p>			Unadjusted	   Adjusted</p>
<p>Latest		  255,463	     256,000</p>
<p>Previous		262,414	     260,600</p>
<p>Year-ago		281,322	     281,800</p>
<p>(No percentages of the total workforce were given.)</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
